  "split": {
    "strategy": "temporal",
    "holdout_fraction": 0.3,
    "explore_n": 12587,
    "holdout_n": 5395,
    "explore_start": "2010-12-01T08:26:00.000000000",
    "explore_end": "2011-09-27T08:57:00.000000000",
    "holdout_start": "2011-09-27T09:05:00.000000000",
    "holdout_end": "2011-12-09T12:50:00.000000000",
    "rationale": "Exploratory / holdout split.\n\nTemporal by default.  Webb (2007, *Discovering Significant Patterns*, Mach.\nLearn. 68:1-33) shows that testing a rule on the same data that suggested it\ninflates the false-discovery rate arbitrarily; the holdout must be untouched\nduring search.  For retail we go further and split on *time*, because a\nrandom split lets December co-purchases vouch for a rule discovered in\nDecember.\n"
  },
